# WolfTune Project Rules

## Tech Stack
- Framework: Next.js 14+ (App Router, TypeScript)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS, Lucide React Icons
- Backend & Database: Supabase (@supabase/ssr, PostgreSQL)
- Integrations: Spotify Web API, Google OAuth
- Deployment: Vercel

## Core Guidelines
1. Write clean, modern, fully typed TypeScript code. Avoid `any`.
2. Follow Next.js App Router best practices (Server Components by default, Client Components only when interactive).
3. Always implement proper error handling and environment variable checks.
4. Keep step-by-step progress: Implement ONE feature at a time, test/verify, then move to the next.
5. Do NOT refactor unrequested files or make breaking structural changes without asking first.
6. Mascot & Theme: "WolfTune" (Dark mode default, accent colors: Blue & Spotify Green). Cute blue wolf mascot used.
7. Styling: Use Tailwind CSS for styling, avoid inline styles.
8. Planning: ask user if in doubts.
